    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "29cf00a4_83831a1f",
        "filename": "system/stack/btm/hfp_lc3_encoder_linux.cc",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 79,
      "author": {
        "id": 2018475
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-28T10:03:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I prefer letting it be a fatal error, or another option: reopen the socket by re-initing the codec client (until it succeeds).\n\nWith correct parameters provided, the transcode only fails when the socket IPC fails. Codec Client needs to be init again to reopen the socket before returning a result.\n\nThe main concern of the second approach is that reopening socket may not solve problem (for example, wrong setting of read/write permission), resulting in an infinite loop.",
      "parentUuid": "3ca67344_605d3015",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 79,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 79,
        "endChar": 12
      },
      "revId": "7973188b3fd4718983260c71e37532a7fdd37c9d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
